.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt OE_SYSCONF 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oe_sysconf_init ,
.Nm oe_sysconf_load ,
.Nm oe_sysconf_free ,
.Nm oe_headers_file_load ,
.Nm oe_attrs_free ,
.Nm oe_env_load_system ,
.Nm oe_service_open ,
.Nm oe_service_close ,
.Nm oe_drop_privileges
.Nd system OpenTelemetry configuration layer of libotelexport
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In oe_sysconf.h
.Ft int
.Fn oe_sysconf_init "struct oe_sysconf *sc"
.Ft int
.Fn oe_sysconf_load "struct oe_sysconf *sc" "const char *defaults_path" "const char *path"
.Ft void
.Fn oe_sysconf_free "struct oe_sysconf *sc"
.Ft int
.Fn oe_headers_file_load "const char *path" "struct oe_attr **attrs" "size_t *n" "char *err" "size_t errlen"
.Ft void
.Fn oe_attrs_free "struct oe_attr *attrs" "size_t n"
.Ft int
.Fn oe_env_load_system "struct oe_env *env" "const struct oe_sysconf *sc" "const char *cli_endpoint"
.Ft int
.Fn oe_service_open "struct oe_service *svc" "const char *service_name" "const char *version" "const char *profile" "const char *cli_endpoint" "double flush_interval" "char *err" "size_t errlen"
.Ft void
.Fn oe_service_close "struct oe_service *svc"
.Ft int
.Fn oe_drop_privileges "const char *user" "char *err" "size_t errlen"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions implement the system layer of the exporter settings
described in
.Xr otel.conf 5 .
The library is internal to the base system.
.Pp
.Fn oe_sysconf_init
fills
.Fa sc
with the built-in defaults.
.Fn oe_sysconf_load
does the same, then reads
.Fa defaults_path
and
.Fa path
over it, then the
.Ic host_id_file
and
.Ic headers_file
they name.
.Dv NULL
selects
.Pa /etc/defaults/otel.conf
and
.Pa /etc/otel.conf ,
or the files named by the environment variables
.Ev OTELCONF_DEFAULTS
and
.Ev OTELCONF_FILE
in programs that are not set-user-ID or set-group-ID;
an empty string skips the layer.
On failure the function stores a message naming the file and the
problem in
.Va sc->error
and leaves the built-in defaults in
.Fa sc .
.Fn oe_sysconf_free
releases the strings held by
.Fa sc .
.Pp
.Fn oe_headers_file_load
reads a credentials file
.Pq see Xr otel.conf 5
into a newly allocated attribute array, released with
.Fn oe_attrs_free .
.Pp
.Fn oe_env_load_system
calls
.Xr oe_env_load 3
and then completes
.Fa env :
.Fa cli_endpoint ,
when not
.Dv NULL ,
replaces the endpoint; settings the environment left unset are taken
from
.Fa sc
when it is enabled; resource attributes and headers are merged by
name with the environment winning.
Headers from the system credentials file are added only if the
resolved endpoint equals
.Va sc->endpoint .
Strings in
.Fa env
may point into
.Fa sc
and
.Fa cli_endpoint ;
release
.Fa env
with
.Xr oe_env_free 3
before freeing
.Fa sc .
.Pp
.Fn oe_service_open
sets up the exporter of a base system telemetry service such as
.Xr otelpfd 8 :
it loads the system configuration, fails if it is invalid or has
.Ic enable
set to false, resolves the settings with
.Fn oe_env_load_system ,
and creates and starts an OTLP exporter in
.Va svc->exporter
whose
.Va service.name
is
.Fa service_name
unless
.Ev OTEL_SERVICE_NAME
is set.
.Fn oe_service_close
flushes and releases everything; it may be called on a
.Fa svc
whose
.Fn oe_service_open
failed.
.Pp
.Fn oe_drop_privileges
permanently changes the process to the user ID, group ID and a group
list consisting of the primary group of
.Fa user ,
and checks that root privileges cannot be regained.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The functions returning
.Vt int
return 0 on success and \-1 on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct oe_sysconf sc;
struct oe_env env;

if (oe_sysconf_load(&sc, NULL, NULL) != 0)
	errx(1, "%s", sc.error);
if (oe_env_load_system(&env, &sc, cli_endpoint) != 0)
	errx(1, "out of memory");
/* env.endpoint may be NULL: use the program default. */
\&...
oe_env_free(&env);
oe_sysconf_free(&sc);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libotelexport 3 ,
.Xr otel.conf 5 ,
.Xr otelauditd 8 ,
.Xr otelconf 8 ,
.Xr otelpfd 8
